## Why This Is Asked
Real-time risk analytics require interpretable, robust dimensionality reduction under nonstationarity. This question tests algorithm design, drift handling, and production latency optimization.

## Key Concepts
- **Online Sparse PCA**: Incremental SVD with L1 penalty to enforce sparsity constraints
- **Drift Detection**: Monitor loadings divergence and reconstruction error for nonstationarity
- **Online Imputation**: Rolling window-based imputation with robust scaling
- **Latency Budgeting**: System-level timing allocation across pipeline stages
- **Evaluation**: Drift scenarios, end-to-end latency profiling, and interpretability validation

## Code Example
```javascript
class OnlineSparsePCA {
  constructor(k, maxNonZeros) {
    this.k = k;
    this.maxNonZeros = maxNonZeros;
    this.components = null;
    this.imputer = new RollingImputer();
    this.scaler = new RobustScaler();
    this.driftMonitor = new DriftMonitor();
  }

  update(x) {
    const t0 = Date.now();
    const xImputed = this.imputer.transform(x);
    const xScaled = this.scaler.transform(xImputed);

    this.components = this.incrementalSparseSVD(xScaled);

    this.driftMonitor.check(this.components, xScaled);

    return { latencies: { impute: t1-t0, scale: t2-t1, svd: t3-t2, total: Date.now()-t0 } };
  }
}
```

